# Held ordinary Windows main-thread entry

This Source-only proposal changes four paths. The actual CLI is `crates/ep_cli/src/main.rs`; the
ordinary history observer is the existing `ep_run` example. Their current `run` bodies, inputs,
solver policies, formulas, outputs, process exit codes, and passive TLS sink construction stay exact.
On Windows GNU/MSVC the existing bodies run on the real main thread. A package-local auto-detected
`build.rs` reserves 8,388,608 bytes in the PE stack header: GNU compiler-driver `-Wl,--stack,8388608`
or MSVC `/STACK:8388608`. Neither flag supplies a commit value or disables stack probes/guards.
The CLI flag targets only `eplus-rs`; Cargo's available examples directive applies to all `ep_run`
examples. Library/test linker flags and `.cargo/config.toml` remain unchanged. Other targets keep
the exact existing 8 MiB worker, join, panic-resume, and spawn-error path. Windows panics unwind
naturally on main; Rust's installed Windows runtime still installs its overflow handler and main
emergency stack guarantee before main. Thread name/backtrace context necessarily becomes main.

The accepted diagnostic observed main/spawn control and endpoint differences for its own binaries.
It does not prove historical production controls or causation. This proposal performs no FP-control
writes and supplies no Native answers. It has not been formatted, built, applied, or executed.
Before acceptance of behavior, build genuine Cargo artifacts, inspect each emitted PE stack reserve
and security/commit fields, run the required same-Source quality commands, and rerun the real CLI and
ordinary observer with unchanged authentic inputs and full output custody. No production PASS or
gate promotion is claimed. Current and historical Source/proof dependencies are explicitly labeled.

Primary build contract references: [Cargo build scripts](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html),
[GNU ld options](https://sourceware.org/binutils/docs/ld/Options.html), and
[MSVC STACK](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/stack-stack-allocations?view=msvc-170).
Cargo detects package-root build.rs without a manifest edit. Target selection reads Cargo's target
environment variables, not build-script host cfg; Cargo-provided target variables do not use
rerun-if-env-changed. This hold adds no dependencies or lock-file changes.
